		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: DM-1701/UV380/UV390 PLUS  +  MDC &amp; Chinese new Firmware]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5023&amp;p=36743#p36743"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>The instructions for using the C6000 state that the audio data buffer is ping-pong accessible, but I couldn't find the corresponding flag, so my method is to read the start bytes of the two buffers, and then compare the newly read data with the old one each time. If there is a difference, it indicates that the other buffer is already readable, and the buffer with changes is storing new data</div></blockquote>Ok. Thanks for the explanation. <br><br>Comparing data bytes is not ideal. Perhaps it would be possible to constantly read all the registers and look for when there are changes which occur at the same repetition rate as the ping pong buffer system.<br><br><br><br>Also... FYI<br><br><br>You should change your code so that you don't use local static variables.<br><br>For the variables that need to persist, make then global to within that individual source code file.<br><br>static global is ok, because all this does is limit access to that global to within that source file.<br><br>But local static is has negative side effects when used with FreeRTOS</div></blockquote>Okay, I will try to learn how to make changes. Thank you for your feedback.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6826">BA7IQE</a> — Sun Apr 13, 2025 11:01 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
